}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T21:07:05-08:00","id":776412,"title":"","content":"Affliction curses a target with maladies. It's a malediction. Are you calling pregnancy a malady?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T22:23:36-08:00","id":776427,"title":"","content":"It allows the ability to inflict persistent conditions which are usually negative in nature and allows any appropriate ST approved condition so I need to figure if a demon could create demon blooded children through virgin birth. or allow normally infertile humans the ability which could result in offspring","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3839-crytofloragardener","name":"CrytofloraGardener","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T22:30:21-08:00","id":776430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CrytofloraGardener</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/776251-question-on-persistent-afflictions?p=776427#post776427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It allows the ability to inflict persistent conditions which are usually negative in nature</div> </div> </div> </div>Understatement writ large.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>The demon curses the target</b>, and may impose one Condition or Tilt. <b>Appropriate choices include Madness, Poisoned, Sick, Shunned, or Mute.</b> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-28T22:34:30-08:00","id":776433,"title":"","content":"So would a near-field gadget be capable of it?<br /> <br /> Edit: Grammar","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3839,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3839-crytofloragardener","user":"CrytofloraGardener","date":". 11-29-2015, 01:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3839-crytofloragardener","name":"CrytofloraGardener","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T00:45:22-08:00","id":776477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CrytofloraGardener</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/776251-question-on-persistent-afflictions?p=776427#post776427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">so I need to figure if a demon could create demon blooded children through virgin birth. or allow normally infertile humans the ability which could result in offspring</div> </div> </div> </div>That absolutely sounds like something an Exploit could do. Just not <i>this</i> Exploit. If homebrewing a virgin birth Exploit is too niche on its own and you wanted to near-field it, I'd look for something like Force Relationship (forging an entire person from fabricated relationships), Halo (a generic soothing blessing type miracle), Inflict Stigmata (a supernatural transforming visitation), or Raise Dead (power over life and rebirth).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T02:46:14-08:00","id":776495,"title":"","content":"Dunno. &quot;I curse you with my demonic seed!!&quot; Sounds maledictive enough. Particularly if the result is something like this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.scp-wiki.net/scp-231\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://scp-wiki.wdfiles.com/local--files/nav:side/social-facebook.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.scp-wiki.net/scp-231\" target=\"_blank\"> SCP-231 - SCP Foundation </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.scp-wiki.net/scp-231\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.scp-wiki.net/scp-231 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> The SCP Foundation's 'top-secret' archives, declassified for your enjoyment. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T08:16:12-08:00","id":776591,"title":"","content":"I think its clear that pregnancy is not an intended use of Affliction. I wouldn't allow it to be used for any other non-negative Condition either. This is a case of trying to twist the power outside of its normal parameters through cherry picking words and ignoring the whole. Trying to force a square peg into a hole that doesn't even exist.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I would also say that Pregnancy should be something that falls under Force Relationship. You are creating a new connection and part of someone's life. That's the domain of messing around with Covers, which is something covered by pacts and certain Mundane Embeds and Mundane-derived Exploits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-29T09:07:38-08:00","id":776619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/776251-question-on-persistent-afflictions?p=776591#post776591\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think its clear that pregnancy is not an intended use of Affliction. I wouldn't allow it to be used for any other non-negative Condition either. This is a case of trying to twist the power outside of its normal parameters through cherry picking words and ignoring the whole. Trying to force a square peg into a hole that doesn't even exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>But that is <i>so</i> Demon. <hr /><br /> Overall, I'd say Affliction might replicate the <i>symptoms</i> (eternal morning sickness, etc.), just not the root cause.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 11-29-2015, 12:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-30T12:13:16-08:00","id":777288,"title":"","content":"what about a a Condition that would not normally be gained by a target such as tagging a normal with the Catalogued or Noted Condition bringing them under God-Machine scrutiny","si